{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE FIRST-VISIT LANGUAGE PROMPT — REFERENCE §7.2
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  One row under the root app bar, asked once: if the browser's first preferred
  language is one we offer and no `ag_lang` cookie has been written, we ask —
  IN THAT LANGUAGE — whether they would like the site in it.

  ── WHY THE ROWS ARE RENDERED AND HIDDEN RATHER THAN BUILT IN JS ─────────────

  `navigator.languages` is only readable in the browser, so the CHOICE of row is
  necessarily client-side. The WORDS are not: each row's question and "yes" come
  from that language's catalogue (`resources/lang/{code}.php`, through
  `Support\Languages::prompts()`), NOT through `|trans` — `|trans` answers in the
  page's language, and this row must ask in the visitor's while the page is still
  English. A language whose catalogue lacks either is not offered, so nothing
  composes a sentence at runtime. Seven small rows is a cheap price for that, and it means the prompt
  works with no JSON blob in an attribute — the shape that silently shredded the
  flier's styles when the HTML parser closed the attribute at the first quote.

  ── EITHER ANSWER SETTLES IT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Both answers are LINKS carrying `?lang=`, which the middleware turns into the
  stored choice. "Keep English" therefore costs a reload of a page that looks
  identical, and that is the price of the prompt working with scripting off and of
  there being exactly one writer for the cookie. The condition for asking is the
  ABSENCE of that cookie, so neither answer can bring the prompt back. A prompt that
  returns is an advert.

  "Keep English" stays in English: it is the option it describes, and somebody who
  wants it can read it.
#}
<div class="ag-langask" data-ag-langask hidden>
  {% for l in lang_prompts() %}
    <div class="ag-langask__row" data-ag-langask-for="{{ l.code }}"
         lang="{{ l.code }}" dir="{{ l.dir }}" hidden>
      <span class="ag-langask__q">{{ l.ask }}</span>
      <a class="ag-btn ag-btn--sm ag-btn--ink" href="{{ lang_url(l.code) }}">{{ l.yes }}</a>
      <a class="ag-btn ag-btn--sm ag-btn--quiet" href="{{ lang_url('en') }}"
         lang="en" dir="ltr">Keep English</a>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
